 "validator": "Validator role (crypto-autoresearcher agents/validator.md), Claude Opus 5.5 subagent. Not the producer of the runs, but launched from the producing Claude Code session (finding F11).",
 "method": "Both binaries' sha256 were checked against aa2_20261029/runs/arms.sha256. Their BLAKE3 was computed with the upstream C reference implementation and checked against software.binary_blake3 in every recorded output. Each binary was then re-run three times, alternating baseline and candidate, one process at a time, with RAYON_NUM_THREADS=1: 'ic price --params research/ic_tool_program/rule/v3/runs/k0n53/T01.params.json --json --out <scratch>' (absolute params path as recorded). Each replay output, each recorded output, and baseline against candidate were compared as canonical JSON (sorted keys) after dropping exactly the keys in keys_dropped: the wall/ns timings and the timing-derived 'units' fields (ns divided by the in-process unit_ns calibration) and the binary hash. ic price writes no host or peak-RSS field. Every other key had to be equal, including the three repetitions' count and every counter, relation count, status, all_verified, recovered and the params path. Across the 126 recorded outputs the dropped keys are exactly the ones that vary. The recovered scalar was verified by verify_scalars.py (Python standard library, no repository code), following benchmarks/20261022-strong-rho-batchinv/verify_scalars.py. It builds GF(2^53) = GF(2)[x]/(x^53+x^6+x^2+x+1) and checks the modulus irreducible (Rabin). On y^2+xy = x^3+1 it checks #E = 9007199311360364 (trace recurrence), r = 21044858204113 prime with r*428 = #E, G on the curve with r*G = O, and the Frobenius eigenvalue. It derives Q from public_hash_seed 23001 by the workflow's BLAKE3 hash-to-curve (its own BLAKE3, self-tested and cross-checked with the C reference on the 62-byte message) and checks that it equals the recorded Q, lies on the curve and is in the subgroup. It then checks d*G == Q for the single d recovered by all 132 recorded and replayed processes, with negative controls (d+1, seed+1).",
